{"reference":"Revelation 19","book":"Revelation","chapter":19,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Interpreting the Marriage Imagery","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The marriage imagery in verses 6–9 has received different theological readings. Jewish interpretation has often read comparable imagery in terms of God and Israel, while Christian readers have connected it with Christ and the church or with the Word and the soul. These are later interpretive traditions, however, rather than identifications explicitly made by the speakers in the passage.","verse_refs":["Revelation 19:6-9"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_019_194dbc2f257b3fc9f1abc9f1"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Revelation’s Scriptural Patterns","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Across Revelation, the book repeatedly reworks imagery and language from Israel’s Scriptures, including Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. This broader pattern helps readers approach its vivid scenes as part of an extensive scriptural conversation rather than as isolated images.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_019_af3a6a0dce88dc3f8f4c44d1"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}